-- ZZ-03-01 (2026-09-15): unify tools.category — closes GitHub issue #282.
--
-- Three incompatible category systems existed before this migration:
--   1. TOOL_DEFINITIONS[].category (src/mcp/tool-definitions.ts) — 25 values, already used
--      by the MCP surface (discover_tools prompt-adapter.ts's categoryIndex).
--   2. static/llms.txt — hand-maintained, 21 values (missing device/logistics/music/podcasts).
--   3. REST /api/v1/tools's old computed 'category' — tool_id.split('.')[0], 398 provider-name
--      prefixes, not a real taxonomy at all (?category=<prefix> filter didn't even exist).
--
-- TOOL_DEFINITIONS[].category is designated the single source of truth (03-SPECIFICATION.md
-- §3 P-2, Fable ruling). This migration:
--   a) adds 'category' (NOT NULL) and backfills it from TOOL_DEFINITIONS, grouped below by
--      category for readability — one UPDATE per of the 25 values, not one CASE per tool_id.
--      Generated from TOOL_DEFINITIONS + config/tool_provider_config.yaml at migration-authoring
--      time (every yaml tool_id has a TOOL_DEFINITIONS entry, verified 2026-09-15 — 0 gaps),
--      not computed at runtime, so this migration has no dependency on application code.
--   b) adds 'namespace' (NOT NULL) and backfills it with the OLD prefix-derived value
--      (tool_id.split('.')[0]) so REST consumers reading the old 'category' semantics keep
--      that value, just renamed — nobody loses access to it (see 05-PROPOSED-FLEET-TASKS.md
--      'что нельзя сломать'). Every tool_id in this table contains a '.' (verified 2026-09-15),
--      so split_part(tool_id, '.', 1) is equivalent to the app-layer's old fallback-to-provider
--      branch for every existing row; a future dot-less tool_id would need that fallback
--      applied at seed time instead (scripts/seed.ts), since this column has no computed
--      default going forward.
--
-- src/services/tool-registry.service.ts's toEntry() switches from the split_part guess to
-- reading these two columns directly; scripts/seed.ts writes both on every upsert from here on.

ALTER TABLE tools ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS category TEXT;
ALTER TABLE tools ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS namespace TEXT;

-- (a) category backfill — one UPDATE per of the 25 TOOL_DEFINITIONS category values.
